  { number := 184, text := "" },
  { number := 185, text := "The key words MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT, RECOMMENDED, MAY, and OPTIONAL in this document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119." },
  { number := 186, text := "" },
  { number := 187, text := "### 3.25 Same word, different trees" },
  { number := 188, text := "" },
  { number := 189, text := "The same English word can name different things in this repository, in Systems Lean, and in companion Lean. Those uses SHALL NOT be treated as the same fact." },
  { number := 190, text := "" },
  { number := 191, text := "1. Systems Lean (Clause 3.18) is the language. Slake (Clause 3.19) is the compiler. The Lake package id `SystemsLean` in the product tree is an internal identifier. It is not a second language name. Prose SHALL say Systems Lean or Slake, not that package id, when naming the language or the compiler." },
  { number := 192, text := "2. The numbered markdown at the repository root is the specification people read. Companion Lean under `lean/` is a meaning model of selected claims. Lean `spec_check` is the form checker. Those three artifacts SHALL NOT be treated as one another. Meaning proofs MUST NOT be treated as a second markdown form checker (Clause 1.2)." },
  { number := 193, text := "3. Residual in this specification is remaining work written in full on disk (Clause 3.7). Residual in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) is a named fact that keeps a product from being fully freestanding. A product tree claim that a freestanding release has no managed Lean leftover is a third use of the word. Those three uses SHALL NOT be treated as the same fact. That product tree claim SHALL NOT be read as this specification having no remaining work." },
  { number := 194, text := "4. The companion Lean meaning model is not a machine learning training run. Recursive self improvement is the loop in Clause 3.14. It is not a claim that a model trains itself again in this repository (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 195, text := "5. Leftover unstack (Clause 3.16) is specified by CATE in [0005_CATE.md](0005_CATE.md). This document does not replace that repair. Leftover unstack remains nonconforming." },
  { number := 196, text := "6. The ASCII word omega in prose is the unrestricted Quantitative Type Theory multiplicity in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md). The companion Lean constructor for that multiplicity is named unrestricted. Authors SHALL NOT write a Greek letter for that multiplicity in this document." },
  { number := 197, text := "7. Scripture named in Clause 1.4 is not a conformance item for Slake, beastdb, or SSSSS (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 198, text := "8. Independent work streams with disjoint write sets SHALL run as parallel tightly scoped agents (Clause 4.7). Running those jobs one after another does not conform." },
  { number := 199, text := "9. Tests are named contracts (Clause 3.5). Observing a failing test for that contract and then editing the product conforms (Clause 4.3). Editing the product and then reshaping the test so it passes without a contract change does not conform." },
  { number := 200, text := "10. This specification is number 0006. CATE is specification [0005](0005_CATE.md) (Clause 1.1 item 4)." },
