  { number := 202, text := "## 4. Core requirements" },
  { number := 203, text := "" },
  { number := 204, text := "### 4.1 Tools that build tools" },
  { number := 205, text := "" },
  { number := 206, text := "1. Agents SHALL prefer improving durable tools (Clause 3.2) over performing a repeated job as a disposable job (Clause 3.3)." },
  { number := 207, text := "2. When a job appears more than once, large language models SHALL be used as tool factories (Clause 3.4): they SHALL produce or improve a durable tool, not only perform the job once." },
  { number := 208, text := "3. Durable tools in this repository SHALL be Lean checkers, project skills, or Nix packages when those can state the check. A probe that is thrown away after one use is not that tool." },
  { number := 209, text := "4. When the encode process itself is improved in the same effort, a Lean checker, a skill step, or a Nix package that proves the improvement is REQUIRED. A chat reminder is not that proof." },
  { number := 210, text := "5. Authors SHALL NOT invent a new Python script or a new shell script as check policy when a Lean checker or a pure Nix evaluation check can state the same rule." },
  { number := 211, text := "" },
  { number := 212, text := "### 4.2 Best tool with reason" },
  { number := 213, text := "" },
  { number := 214, text := "1. Language purity is not ideology. Authors and agents SHALL use the best available tool that can state the theorem or the contract (Clause 3.13)." },
  { number := 215, text := "2. When that substrate exists, that tool MAY be CompCert C (Clause 3.22), Rust, or Systems Lean as specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md)." },
  { number := 216, text := "3. Authors SHALL NOT use bash or Python as check policy in Nix. Form rules for numbered specifications remain Lean `spec_check`. Trailing whitespace and tab indent across this repository remain pure Nix evaluation as in [0000_spec.md](0000_spec.md) Clause 17.1." },
  { number := 217, text := "4. Authors and agents SHALL discard a broken tool rather than keep it because it is familiar." },
  { number := 218, text := "5. When a stronger tool can state the theorem, authors SHALL use that tool. They SHALL NOT fall back to a weaker testing workflow because it is familiar or looks smaller." },
  { number := 219, text := "" },
  { number := 220, text := "### 4.3 Failing tests first" },
  { number := 221, text := "" },
  { number := 222, text := "1. For behavior changes and bug fixes, authors and agents SHALL observe a failing test in the product tree for the named contract (Clause 3.5) before the product edit that is meant to make that same test pass (Clause 3.6)." },
  { number := 223, text := "2. Tests are contracts. When the intended contract changes, authors SHALL reconcile that change with the numbered specification in the same effort. When RSI is the specification that changed, they SHALL reconcile with this document." },
  { number := 224, text := "3. Authors SHALL NOT reshape a test so it passes without a contract change." },
  { number := 225, text := "4. Authors SHALL NOT delete or weaken a test to finish green when the named contract has not changed." },
  { number := 226, text := "5. Green without a prior observed failing test for that named contract is not the proof order this clause requires." },
  { number := 227, text := "" },
  { number := 228, text := "### 4.4 Ambiguity and truth seeking" },
  { number := 229, text := "" },
  { number := 230, text := "1. When intent is ambiguous, authors and agents SHALL stop and ask in ordinary American English." },
  { number := 231, text := "2. A question to a human SHALL name the file or clause, quote the current wording, say why the choice matters, name the options, use ordinary English, define a new phrase in the same sentence when one is introduced, and say what we will do for each option, as required by [0005_CATE.md](0005_CATE.md)." },
  { number := 232, text := "3. Authors and agents SHALL prove assumptions. They SHALL NOT rely on unstated heuristics." },
  { number := 233, text := "4. Authors and agents SHALL seek the truth of the work (Clause 3.15). They SHALL NOT pad an unknown with leftover guesses presented as findings." },
  { number := 234, text := "5. When they do not know why something fails, they SHALL say they do not know, name what they ruled out, and ask for the fact that would distinguish remaining causes." },
  { number := 235, text := "" },
  { number := 236, text := "### 4.5 Attention and remaining work" },
  { number := 237, text := "" },
  { number := 238, text := "1. Authors and agents SHALL plan with pointers on disk: residual clauses, `lean/ResidualClaims.lean`, reports under the operator report home, and project skills." },
  { number := 239, text := "2. Remaining work SHALL be written in full in complete American English sentences (Clause 3.7). Chat is not the residual record." },
  { number := 240, text := "3. A later session SHALL be able to continue from those pointers without reconstructing intent from chat." },
  { number := 241, text := "4. Prose SHALL be concise natural language. Authors SHALL NOT use decoder ring jargon. Help the next session." },
  { number := 242, text := "5. Silence about unpublished specifications, unassigned numbers, unpinned prior art, unimplemented requirements, or out of scope items this document names is nonconforming for this specification as a document. Residual is Clause 6." },
  { number := 243, text := "" },
  { number := 244, text := "### 4.6 Self improvement loop" },
  { number := 245, text := "" },
  { number := 246, text := "1. Recursive self improvement in this specification is the loop in Clause 3.14: improve durable tools, prove them, keep residual honest, run independent streams in parallel, and ask when intent is ambiguous." },
  { number := 247, text := "2. This specification MUST NOT be read as a claim that a model trains itself again in this repository." },
  { number := 248, text := "3. Inference that tests training, in the sense of this document, is that loop. It is not a training run stored in this tree." },
  { number := 249, text := "4. This document MAY later be input to SSSP (Clause 3.11). SSSP has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 250, text := "" },
  { number := 251, text := "### 4.7 Parallel independent streams" },
  { number := 252, text := "" },
  { number := 253, text := "1. Independent work streams (Clause 3.8) SHALL run as parallel tightly scoped agents (Clause 3.10) when those streams do not share a write set (Clause 3.9)." },
  { number := 254, text := "2. Authors and agents SHALL NOT run two jobs one after the other when those jobs do not share a write set." },
  { number := 255, text := "3. When two numbered specifications must land in one effort, authors SHALL spawn one tightly scoped agent per specification on disjoint files." },
  { number := 256, text := "4. Files that more than one stream must change SHALL be updated in one later pass, not raced by parallel writers." },
  { number := 257, text := "5. A new ask that does not share a write set with a healthy live stream SHALL run in parallel. It SHALL NOT cancel that live stream unless the operator said to stop." },
  { number := 258, text := "" },
  { number := 259, text := "### 4.8 Remote builder practice" },
  { number := 260, text := "" },
  { number := 261, text := "1. When this document talks about proving tests that compile, those tests SHALL run on a remote builder if the project already requires that builder (Clause 3.12)." },
  { number := 262, text := "2. If that builder is unresponsive, authors and agents SHALL stop rather than invent a weaker local compile as the proof." },
  { number := 263, text := "3. This specifications repository's validation gate remains `nix flake check` as in [0000_spec.md](0000_spec.md). That gate is not a Rust cargo harness." },
  { number := 264, text := "4. `bitmask-core`, `bitmask-next`, and RGB are out of scope as product. This document SHALL NOT treat those trees as deliverables." },
  { number := 265, text := "5. Practice about a remote builder is not a specification of bitmask products. This document SHALL NOT be read as a bitmask specification." },
  { number := 266, text := "" },
  { number := 267, text := "### 4.9 Scripture is not a compiler test" },
  { number := 268, text := "" },
  { number := 269, text := "1. Scripture named in Clause 1.4 MUST NOT be a conformance item for Slake, beastdb, or SSSSS." },
  { number := 270, text := "2. An implementation MUST NOT be judged conforming or nonconforming by citation of scripture." },
  { number := 271, text := "3. Authors SHALL NOT expand Clause 1.4 into theology in this document or in a later numbered specification without an explicit operator ask." },
  { number := 272, text := "4. The informative naming in Clause 1.4 MUST NOT be treated as a proven cosmology." },
  { number := 273, text := "" },
  { number := 274, text := "### 4.10 Same word, different trees" },
  { number := 275, text := "" },
  { number := 276, text := "1. Authors and agents SHALL keep the distinctions in Clause 3.25 when the same English word appears in more than one tree." },
  { number := 277, text := "2. Authors SHALL NOT treat Systems Lean, Slake, and the Lake package id `SystemsLean` as one name." },
  { number := 278, text := "3. Authors SHALL NOT treat the numbered markdown, the companion Lean meaning model, and `spec_check` as one artifact." },
  { number := 279, text := "4. Authors SHALL NOT treat remaining work on disk, a named freestanding blocker in Systems Lean, and a product tree claim that a freestanding release has no managed Lean leftover as one residual fact." },
  { number := 280, text := "5. Authors SHALL NOT treat the companion Lean meaning model as a machine learning training run." },
  { number := 281, text := "6. Authors SHALL NOT replace leftover unstack as specified in [0005_CATE.md](0005_CATE.md)." },
  { number := 282, text := "7. Authors SHALL write the unrestricted multiplicity as the ASCII word omega in prose. They SHALL name the companion Lean constructor unrestricted." },
  { number := 283, text := "8. Independent work streams with disjoint writes MUST run in parallel. Serializing them does not conform (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 284, text := "9. A failing test then a product edit conforms. A product edit then reshaping the test does not conform (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 285, text := "10. Companion Lean under `lean/` encodes those distinctions. That encoding is a meaning model. It is not this specification." },
  { number := 286, text := "" },
  { number := 287, text := "### 4.11 Meaning models in this repository" },
  { number := 288, text := "" },
  { number := 289, text := "1. Authors and agents who prove companion Lean meaning models under `lean/` in this repository SHALL follow the project skill `/lean4` at `.agents/skills/lean4/SKILL.md`." },
  { number := 290, text := "2. That skill points at the Lean 4 agent skill pack git submodule at `skills/lean4-skills`. That pack is not a Clause 12 pin. That pack is not under `ref/`. That pack is not `mathlib`." },
  { number := 291, text := "3. This Lake package SHALL NOT add `mathlib`." },
  { number := 292, text := "4. Shipped theorems SHALL NOT contain `sorry`." },
  { number := 293, text := "" },
  { number := 294, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
  { number := 295, text := "" },
  { number := 296, text := "Work in this repository conforms to this specification if and only if all of the following hold:" },
  { number := 297, text := "" },
  { number := 298, text := "1. Durable tools are preferred over a disposable job when the job repeats, a repeated job is turned into or improved as a tool rather than only performed once, and an encode process improvement is proved by a Lean checker, a skill step, or a Nix package rather than by a chat reminder (Clause 4.1)." },
  { number := 299, text := "2. The best available tool that can state the theorem or the contract is used; bash and Python are not used as check policy in Nix; a broken tool is discarded; a stronger tool that can state the theorem is not skipped because a weaker workflow is familiar (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 300, text := "3. For behavior changes, a failing test in the product tree for the named contract is observed before the product edit that is meant to make that same test pass, and contract changes are reconciled with the numbered specification, with this document when RSI is that specification (Clause 4.3)." },
  { number := 301, text := "4. Ambiguous intent is stopped on and asked about with a question that names the file or clause, quotes the current wording, says why the choice matters, and names the options; assumptions are proved; unstated heuristics are not relied on; leftover guesses are not presented as findings (Clause 4.4)." },
  { number := 302, text := "5. Remaining work is written in full on disk in complete American English; chat is not treated as the residual record; a later session can continue from those pointers (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 303, text := "6. Recursive self improvement is treated as the loop in Clause 4.6, not as a claim that a model trains itself again in this repository, and this document is not treated as specifying SSSP (Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 304, text := "7. Independent work streams that do not share a write set run as parallel tightly scoped agents; jobs that do not share a write set are not forced to wait on each other; shared files are updated in one later pass (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 305, text := "8. When proving tests that compile for a project that already requires a remote builder, those tests run on that builder, and work stops if that builder is unresponsive; `bitmask-core`, `bitmask-next`, and RGB are not treated as deliverables of this document (Clause 4.8)." },
  { number := 306, text := "9. Scripture named in Clause 1.4 is not treated as a conformance item for Slake, beastdb, or SSSSS, and is not treated as a proven cosmology (Clause 4.9)." },
  { number := 307, text := "10. The same English word used in more than one tree is kept distinct as in Clause 3.25 and Clause 4.10." },
  { number := 308, text := "11. Authors and agents who prove companion Lean meaning models follow the project skill `/lean4`; this Lake package does not add `mathlib`; shipped theorems do not contain `sorry` (Clause 4.11)." },
  { number := 309, text := "" },
  { number := 310, text := "The informative naming in Clause 1.4 is not a conformance item." },
  { number := 311, text := "" },
  { number := 312, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming implementation. Meeting these items is a claim about work in this repository, not about this markdown file." },
  { number := 313, text := "" },
  { number := 314, text := "## 6. Residual" },
  { number := 315, text := "" },
  { number := 316, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. It does not add product behavior beyond Clauses 4 and 5. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unnumbered substrate, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope item named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. Checkable residual claims live in `lean/ResidualClaims.lean`, and this specification still carries its own residual clause." },
  { number := 317, text := "" },
  { number := 318, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 319, text := "" },
  { number := 320, text := "1. The Surmount Systems System Prompt (SSSP) is named in Scope as possible later input to that prompt. SSSP has no assigned specification number. This document does not create a numbered file for SSSP. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 321, text := "2. fargo has no assigned specification number. This document does not create a numbered file for fargo. A previous plan that assigned number [0005](0005_CATE.md) to fargo is withdrawn. This document does not invent a new number for fargo. This document does not steal 0006 for fargo. [0003_beastdb.md](0003_beastdb.md) still names fargo as the interoperability path; that is a requirement on a future product, not a claim that fargo is specified or implemented. [0004_SSSSS.md](0004_SSSSS.md) does not require fargo." },
  { number := 322, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Number 0005 is CATE ([0005_CATE.md](0005_CATE.md)). Number 0006 is this specification (RSI), not Carbonado. This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 323, text := "" },
  { number := 324, text := "### 6.2 Holy Lean, Legal Lean, and Bio Lean have no assigned specification numbers" },
  { number := 325, text := "" },
  { number := 326, text := "1. Lean Machine is specified in [0013_Lean_Machine.md](0013_Lean_Machine.md). That document is specification 0013." },
  { number := 327, text := "2. Holy Lean, Legal Lean, and Bio Lean are names only. They are not numbered specifications. This document does not create files for them." },
  { number := 328, text := "3. A Lean Machine that persists as a shared pattern is named only in this document. Lean Machine itself is specified in [0013_Lean_Machine.md](0013_Lean_Machine.md). This document does not restate that specification." },
  { number := 329, text := "" },
  { number := 330, text := "### 6.3 Out of scope product trees" },
  { number := 331, text := "" },
  { number := 332, text := "1. `bitmask-core`, `bitmask-next`, and RGB are not Surmount numbered specifications. They are out of scope for this file as product. Practice about remote builders or tests that compile is not a specification of those trees." },
  { number := 333, text := "" },
  { number := 334, text := "### 6.4 Unimplemented product claims" },
  { number := 335, text := "" },
  { number := 336, text := "1. This document specifies RSI. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that every agent already conforms. Treating a chat reminder as a durable tool is Cons False in the RSI proofs module. Treating recursive self improvement as a claim that a model trains itself again in this repository is Cons False in that same module. Treating every agent as already conforming is Cons False in that same module. Treating independent work streams with disjoint write sets as run one after another is Cons False in that same module. Treating a product edit then reshaping the test without a contract change as conforming is Cons False in that same module. Treating leftover unstack as this specification is Cons False in that same module. Treating this document as a bitmask specification is Cons False in that same module. Treating chat as the residual record is Cons False in that same module. Treating meaning proofs as a second form checker is Cons False in that same module." },
  { number := 337, text := "2. SSSP has no assigned specification number. This document does not create a numbered file for SSSP. Treating this document as creating SSSP is Cons False in the RSI proofs module. Treating SSSP as numbered is Cons False in that same module." },
  { number := 338, text := "3. A remote builder named by some other Surmount project is not a deliverable of this file." },
  { number := 339, text := "4. Clause 4 states requirements on authors and agents. This document does not claim those requirements are already met by every session. Treating those requirements as already met by every session is Cons False in the RSI proofs module." },
  { number := 340, text := "" },
  { number := 341, text := "### 6.5 Informative items this document names" },
  { number := 342, text := "" },
  { number := 343, text := "1. Clause 1.4 is informative. Scripture is not a conformance item for Slake, beastdb, or SSSSS. Scripture is not a proven cosmology. Those texts are not Clause 12 pins." },
  { number := 344, text := "2. CATE is specified in [0005_CATE.md](0005_CATE.md). CATE is not this specification. CATE was first written as Clause 20 of [0000_spec.md](0000_spec.md); that placement is history." },
  { number := 345, text := "3. Continuous Integration is specified in [0007_CI.md](0007_CI.md). That document is not this specification. Number 0007 is not RSI." },
  { number := 346, text := "" },
  { number := 347, text := "### 6.6 Vocabulary maps this document does not import" },
  { number := 348, text := "" },
  { number := 349, text := "1. This document does not restate bootstrap stages from the Systems Lean product tree." },
  { number := 350, text := "2. This document does not import security term maps from other Surmount projects as process vocabulary." },
  { number := 351, text := "3. Companion Lean under `lean/Vocabulary.lean` is a meaning model of Clause 3.25. It is not this specification." },
  { number := 352, text := "" },
  { number := 353, text := "### 6.7 Lean 4 agent skill pack" },
  { number := 354, text := "" },
  { number := 355, text := "1. The git submodule at `skills/lean4-skills` is the Lean 4 agent skill pack. It is original work under the `MIT` license. It is not Unlicense. It is not a Clause 12 pin. It is not under `ref/`. It is not `mathlib`. This Lake package does not add `mathlib`." },
  { number := 356, text := "2. Following `/lean4` is a requirement of Clause 4.11. This document does not claim every agent already follows it." },
  { number := 357, text := "" },
  { number := 358, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
  { number := 359, text := "" },
  { number := 360, text := "### 0.1.0 - 20260831" },
  { number := 361, text := "" },
  { number := 362, text := "Current version line is 0.1.0 by operator order. Changelog history records that a 1.1.0 line existed. This same 0.1.0 line records that continued improvement of the Supercompiler is this specification's loop together with delta reconciliation in [0004_SSSSS.md](0004_SSSSS.md), and that improvement is not claimed finished." },
  { number := 363, text := "" },
  { number := 364, text := "### 1.1.0 - 20260825" },
  { number := 365, text := "" },
  { number := 366, text := "Renumbers this specification to 0006 with file name `0006_RSI.md`. Concise American Technical English is specified in [0005_CATE.md](0005_CATE.md). CATE is specification 0005. This specification is not CATE. Number 0006 is RSI, not Carbonado." },
  { number := 367, text := "" },
  { number := 368, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260825" },
  { number := 369, text := "" },
  { number := 370, text := "First publication of this specification text. That 1.0.0 assigned this document number 0005; version 1.1.0 corrects the stack number to 0006. Records that Concise American Technical English is specified in [0005_CATE.md](0005_CATE.md) (CATE was first written as Clause 20 of [0000_spec.md](0000_spec.md); that placement is history; [0000_spec.md](0000_spec.md) points at [0005_CATE.md](0005_CATE.md) for CATE); withdraws the previous plan that assigned number 0005 to fargo; requires durable tools over a disposable job and requires large language models to act as factories that produce or improve tools when a job will repeat; requires the best available tool that can state a theorem or a contract, including CompCert C, Rust, or Systems Lean when that substrate exists, and including that bash and Python are not check policy in Nix; requires a failing test in the product tree for a named contract before the product edit that is meant to make that same test pass; requires stopping and asking on ambiguity and proving assumptions; requires remaining work written in full on disk in complete American English; requires independent work streams with disjoint writes to run as parallel tightly scoped agents; states that recursive self improvement is that loop and not a claim that a model trains itself again in this repository; names this document as possible later input to SSSP while stating that SSSP has no assigned specification number; requires tests that compile to run on a remote builder when the project already requires that builder, and to stop if that builder is unresponsive; and states that scripture named here is inspiration for honorable society, not a proven cosmology, and is not a conformance item for Slake, beastdb, or SSSSS." },
  { number := 371, text := "" },
  { number := 372, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: fargo has no assigned number; Lean Machine is specified as [0013_Lean_Machine.md](0013_Lean_Machine.md); Holy Lean, Legal Lean, and Bio Lean remain without separate numbered specifications; a Lean Machine that persists as a shared pattern is named only; the Carbonado Network Protocol has no assigned number; `bitmask-core`, `bitmask-next`, and RGB are out of scope as product." },
  { number := 373, text := "" },
  { number := 374, text := "This unpublished 1.0.0 also records that hyphenated modifiers in prose were rephrased into ordinary English. Deleting the hyphen and leaving the same two words is not enough." },
  { number := 375, text := "" },
  { number := 376, text := "This unpublished 1.0.0 also expands definitions, core requirements, and the conformance if and only if clause so this document is a complete specification of that loop rather than a short first draft." },
  { number := 377, text := "" },
  { number := 378, text := "This unpublished 1.0.0 also records the same English word used in more than one tree: Systems Lean is the language, Slake is the compiler, and the Lake package id `SystemsLean` is not a second language name; numbered markdown is the contract humans read, Lean spec encodings state what must be true, Lean proofs are separate modules, and `spec_check` is the form checker; remaining work on disk is not Systems Lean residual and is not a product tree claim that a freestanding release has no managed Lean leftover; leftover unstack stays CATE; the ASCII word omega maps to the Lean constructor unrestricted; independent streams with disjoint writes run in parallel; a failing test then a product edit conforms and reshaping a test after the product edit does not." },
  { number := 379, text := "" },
  { number := 380, text := "This unpublished 1.0.0 also records that agents who prove companion Lean meaning models in this repository SHALL follow the project skill `/lean4` at `.agents/skills/lean4/SKILL.md`, which points at the Lean 4 agent skill pack submodule at `skills/lean4-skills`." },
